  <aggregations>
    <task override="true">
      <composition>
        <workflow:InstructionTask>
        <instructions>
        Create a small library domain model in package `org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.library`.

The model shall represent a library that manages books and registered members.

A book has a title, an ISBN, and an availability status. A book can have one or more authors.

A member has a name and a unique member number.

Model the concept of borrowing explicitly. A borrowing connects a member with a book and records when the book was borrowed and when it is due.

The model shall express the following rules and semantics through appropriate BlockML structures:

* A book can only be borrowed by one member at a time.
* A member can have multiple active borrowings.
* Authors exist independently of books and may have written multiple books.
* A borrowing belongs to the library's managed state and is not merely a property of a book or member.

Choose appropriate blocks, types, properties, associations, and aggregations based on the semantics of the domain.

Add concise documentation to the important blocks explaining their purpose.

The resulting model must be valid BlockML.

        </instructions>
        </workflow:InstructionTask>
      </composition>
    </task>
  </aggregations>
</block>